WEBVTT

00:18:57.324 --> 00:19:00.440
So, maybe over 10 years ago
now, our library got flooded.

00:19:00.464 --> 00:19:02.515
This is before the Internet
got really big.

00:19:02.539 --> 00:19:05.220
And I was really upset
about all the books being wrecked,

00:19:05.244 --> 00:19:07.220
because it was knowledge being destroyed.

00:19:07.244 --> 00:19:11.657
And server farms, or data centers,
are great libraries of knowledge.

00:19:11.681 --> 00:19:12.972
CA: Temple, can I just say,

00:19:12.996 --> 00:19:15.082
it's an absolute delight
to have you at TED.

00:19:15.106 --> 00:19:16.257
Thank you so much.

00:19:16.281 --> 00:19:18.176
TG: Well, thank you so much. Thank you.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:23.436
(Applause)